# SECTION – A (Compulsory)

## 1 (a) - 20 marks

**1) Choose the correct option:** [15 × 2=30]

### 1 (a) (i) - 2 marks

Cost Audit was first introduced in the year______:

- (A) 1959
- (B) 1965
- (C) 1949
- (D) 1975

### 1 (a) (ii) - 2 marks

As per Companies (Cost Records and Audit) Rules, 2014 which of the following Sector comes under Non-Regulated Sector?

- (A) Drugs and Pharmaceuticals
- (B) Fertilisers
- (C) Sugar and Industrial Alcohol
- (D) Cement

### 1 (a) (iii) - 2 marks

Variances due to abnormal reasons _______________form part of cost as per GACAP.

- (A) Will not
- (B) Is
- (C) Are
- (D) Will

### 1 (a) (iv) - 2 marks

Cost Accounting standard 18 is a Cost Accounting Standard on __________

- (A) Royalty and Technical Knowhow fee.
- (B) Material cost
- (C) Research and Development Cost
- (D) Financial Cost

### 1 (a) (v) - 2 marks

The overall objectives of the Independent Cost Auditor and ensuring audit in accordance with Cost Accounting Standards is laid down in Cost Auditing Standards ____

- (A) 101
- (B) 102
- (C) 103
- (D) 104

### 1 (a) (vi) - 2 marks

Which of the following is not involved in the Planning Stage of Audit Process?

- (A) Gaining an understanding of the client
- (B) Detailed testing of Internal Controls
- (C) Identifying factors that may impact the risk of material misstatement in Cost Statements
- (D) Developing an audit strategy

### 1 (a) (vii) - 2 marks

XBRL is the abbreviated form of __________.

- (A) eXtensible Business Reporting Language
- (B) eXtensive Business Reporting Language
- (C) eXtended Business Reporting Language
- (D) None of the above.

### 1 (a) (viii) - 2 marks

Which of the following type of Internal Control is designed to keep errors or irregularities from occurring in the first place.

- (A) Corrective Control
- (B) Detective Control
- (C) Monitoring Control
- (D) Preventive Control

### 1 (a) (ix) - 2 marks

Test checking is done when there is an effective system of

- (A) Internal control
- (B) Internal Audit
- (C) Internal check
- (D) Both A and B

### 1 (a) (x) - 2 marks

The Tool used in Forensic auditing that explains three inter related elements – Pressure, Opportunity and Realisation, that assist the Commission of fraud:

- (A) Fraud Triangle
- (B) Fraud Tree
- (C) Fraud Model
- (D) Fraud Square

## 1 (b) - 10 marks

**Choose the Correct Option:** (2 x 5 = 10)

LMN Co. has planned an investment of ₹900.00 lakh, out of which 60% will be financed through a bank loan carrying an interest rate of 12% p.a.

The Direct Cost for the year is ₹520.00 lakh, of which 55% represents Material Cost. Other operating expenses are estimated at ₹95.00 lakh.

The company plans to sell the goods at 160% of the Direct Cost. Depreciation on fixed assets is 10% of total investment. Selling expenses are estimated at 5% of Sales. The applicable tax rate is assumed to be 45%.

You are required to indicate the correct option for the following:

### 1 (b) (xi) - 2 marks

Return on Investment is:

- (A) 1.26%
- (B) 1.36%
- (C) 2.29%
- (D) 3.15%

### 1 (b) (xii) - 2 marks

Return on Assets is:

- (A) 1.26%
- (B) 1.36%
- (C) 2.29%
- (D) 3.15%

### 1 (b) (xiii) - 2 marks

Return on Owner’s Equity is:

- (A) 1.26%
- (B) 1.36%
- (C) 2.29%
- (D) 3.15%

### 1 (b) (xiv) - 2 marks

Assets Turnover Ratio is:

- (A) 0.89
- (B) 0.90
- (C) 0.91
- (D) 0.92

### 1 (b) (xv) - 2 marks

Inventory Turnover Ratio is:

- (A) 33.33%
- (B) 34.38%
- (C) 23.25%
- (D) 24.27%

