# SECTION – B

**Answer any 5 questions out of 7 questions given. Each question carries 14 marks.** [5 × 14 = 70]

## 2 (a) - 7 marks

Explain Cost Accounting Standards and its benefits. [7]

## 2 (b) - 7 marks

As per the Companies (Cost Records and Audit) Rules, 2014, Describe the particulars relating to the items of costs to be included in the Books of Accounts in respect of Royalty and Technical Know-how. [7]

## 3 (a) - 7 marks

Explain the provisions of fixing the remuneration of Cost Auditor as per the Companies Act, 2013 and rules thereunder. [7]

## 3 (b) - 7 marks

Discuss the checklist that should be kept in view to audit electricity cost generated by DG Set during cost audit. [7]

## 4 (a) - 7 marks

Purchase of Materials ₹ 5,00,000 (inclusive of GST of ₹ 26,150); Free on Board ₹ 24,000; Import Duty paid ₹ 20,000; Freight inward ₹ 30,000; Insurance paid for import by sea ₹15,000; Rebates allowed ₹ 5,000; Cash discount ₹ 4,000; Subsidy received from the Government for importation of these materials ₹ 30,000. Calculate the landed cost of material (i.e. value of receipt of material). [7]

## 4 (b) - 7 marks

The following particulars pertaining to production of yarn are extracted from the records of MN Ltd., for the year ended on March 31,2026:

| Particulars | ₹ ‘000 |
|---|---:|
| Direct Material Cost | 3,560 |
| Direct Wages and Salaries | 2,450 |
| Direct Expenses | 560 |
| Indirect Materials | 670 |
| Factory Overheads | 965 |
| Administrative Overheads (45% relating to production activities) | 1,450 |
| Quality control cost | 625 |
| Research and Development Cost | 700 |
| Interest on Working Capital (12% on ₹50,00,000) | 600 |
| Sale of Scrap Realised | 570 |

You are required to Calculate the cost of production for the purpose of captive consumption in terms of the Rule 30 of the Central Goods and Service Tax Rules, 2017 and as per the CAS-4 (Revised) and the Assessable Value for the purpose of paying GST on applicable transactions. [7]

## 5 (a) - 7 marks

The financial profit and loss account for the year 2025-26 of a company shows a net profit of ₹ 35,50,000. During the course of Cost Audit, it was noticed that:

- (i) The company was engaged in trading activity earning a profit for ₹ 3,70,000.
- (ii) Some discarded assets sold off with no residual book value for ₹ 2,60,800.
- (iii) Some renovation of machinery was carried out at a cost of ₹ 12,00,000, having a productive life of five years, but no amount was charged to cost accounts.
- (iv) Interest was received amounting to ₹ 4,50,600 from various investments.
- (v) Voluntary Retirement payment of ₹ 3,50,000 was not included in the Cost Accounts. (should 50% amortized)
- (vi) Insurance claim of previous year was received to the extent of ₹ 3,50,000 but was not considered in the Cost Accounts.
- (vii) Decrease in Closing stock of finished goods & WIP over opening inventory was ₹ 2,10,000 in the financial accounts, and ₹ 95,000 in the Cost Accounts.
- (viii) Donation of ₹ 2,80,000 towards CSR commitment was not considered in the Cost Accounts.

Identify the profit as per the Cost Accounts. [7]

